From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:12:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] adbd: let any host in when built for the initramfs debug
 shell

The Halium initramfs's debug shell (INITRAMFS_DEBUG_SHELL = "1") starts
adbd when the boot fails, so that a phone with a black screen can still
be reached. LuneOS's adbd asks org.webosports.service.devmode about every
host it has no key for, and refuses the host when nobody answers. The
initramfs has neither that service nor /var/lib/adbd/adb_keys, so that
adbd refused every host and the debug shell was reachable by telnet only.

With LUNEOS_ADBD_ANY_KEY defined, adbd does not ask for authorisation, as
Debian's own adbd does on Linux. Only the second adbd that android-tools
builds for the initramfs, adbd-initramfs, defines it, and only in builds
with the debug shell; the rootfs's adbd is built as before.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific: initramfs debug builds only]
---
 packages/modules/adb/daemon/main.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/modules/adb/daemon/main.cpp b/packages/modules/adb/daemon/main.cpp
--- a/packages/modules/adb/daemon/main.cpp
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/daemon/main.cpp
@@ -256,6 +256,11 @@
         auth_required = android::base::GetBoolProperty("ro.adb.secure", false);
 #endif
     }
+#elif defined(LUNEOS_ADBD_ANY_KEY)
+    // The initramfs debug shell's adbd (android-tools-adbd-initramfs): the
+    // initramfs has no developer mode service to ask and no adb_keys, so
+    // with authorisation on it could let nobody in.
+    auth_required = false;
 #endif
 
     // Our external storage path may be different than apps, since
